       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. That's well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day, and some institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A 2,000 mg single dose is also double the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. Even with normal liver function, this dose risks hepatotoxicity.\n\nHere are some standard options:\n- **1000 mg orally three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg orally four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg orally every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf 2000 mg three times daily was a typo, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you meant it, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'll add it to the order note."
